# 2026-10-07: removed the brace-expansion/browserslist/fast-uri/js-yaml entries
# (exp 2026-10-09). They were already cleared by version-scoped pnpm.overrides
# on 2026-09-16; a current `trivy fs` of pnpm-lock.yaml no longer reports them.

# zod 3.x (3.23.8 / 3.25.76) -> fixed only in 4.6.6 (CVE-2023-54404 = GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5,
# "exhaust memory while validating oversized constrained collections"). Owner-approved dated
# exception (2026-10-24), the same as scripts/ci/cve-allowlist.json: request bodies are capped
# (explicit Fastify bodyLimit on every service, enforced by scripts/ci/fastify-bodylimit-guard.mjs),
# so no collection can reach a memory-exhausting size. The real fix is the zod 3->4 major upgrade
# across ~70 packages, scheduled post-release. The dev-only zod 4.6.5 copy is already patched to 4.6.6.
CVE-2023-54404 exp:2026-11-23
GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5 exp:2026-11-23

# 2026-10-26 (codescan/trivy-base-image): Debian 12.15 OS-layer CVEs with NO fixed
# version. Base image is already the latest node 20.x bookworm-slim
# (20.20.2, 2026-04-22) and the runtime stage runs apt-get upgrade, so no
# newer base/patch exists to bump to. Verified with a full trivy scan of the
# built gateway image: 0 fixable OS CRITICAL/HIGH; the 14 IDs below are all
# unfixed in Debian (status shown). Package sets: util-linux family
# (bsdutils/libblkid1/libmount1/libsmartcols1/libuuid1/mount/util-linux/
# util-linux-extra), ncurses, libsystemd0/libudev1, gzip, libacl1, wget,
# perl-base, zlib1g. All are Debian-essential/dpkg-required or the healthcheck
# wget; the container runs non-root with no shell-exposed network service.
# Revisit when Debian ships fixes; expires 2026-12-31 so it cannot go stale.

# zlib1g minizip overflow - Debian will_not_fix (not exploitable via node runtime)
CVE-2023-45853 exp:2026-12-31
# ncurses - affected, no fix yet
